# Level 12 → 13

## Goal
Find the password hidden inside multiple nested layers of compression, starting from a hexdump 
of a file that has been compressed repeatedly using different formats (gzip, bzip2, tar, etc.).

## Commands used
```bash
# Setup scratch workspace
mkdir /tmp/mywork12
cp data.txt /tmp/mywork12
cd /tmp/mywork12

# Step 1 - reverse the hexdump back to binary
xxd -r data.txt > data

# Step 2 - check file type, rename, decompress (repeat until ASCII text)
file data
mv data data.gz
gzip -d data.gz

file data
mv data data.bz2
bzip2 -df data.bz2

file data
tar -xf data.tar
ls

# keep repeating file → rename → decompress until:      # shows: ASCII text


## My decompression sequence
1. xxd -r → gzip
2. gzip -d → bzip2
3. bzip2 -d → tar
4. tar -xf → gzip
5. gzip -d → ASCII text 

